    "scenesThatPass": [
      "MARY: Not the eldest daughter?\nMARY: Best be wary of her. It is said the girl is the child of a forest witch. They say she is passing strange, touched, perhaps mad.\nELIZA: I have seen her once, wandering the backroads at will, with a hawk on her arm -\nMARY: A hawk. At Hewlands?",
      "AGNES: Two of you..\nMARY: Agnes, come to the stool. It is ready. It is here. We shall help you.\nAGNES: ...Two of you standing at my deathbed...I always thought they would be my children..it turns out to be you...",
      "AGNES: ...Why isn’t she crying?\nMARY: She lives not.\nAGNES: Let me have her...",
      "SUSANNA: We all know they’ve swapped clothes. How long are we going to pretend we don’t?\nAGNES: We shall pretend for as long as they still think they are the same -",
      "JUDITH: When the hurly-bu rly’s done, when the battle’s lost and won.\nSUSANNA: That will be ere the set of sun."
    ]
  },
